Repair chunking review defects. Read AGENTS.md, .agents/AGENTS.md,
doc/chunking.md and doc/chunking-evaluation.md, and repair rules in
doc/manual-workflow.md and doc/automated-workflow.md.

```sh
RUN_ID="your-reviewed-run-id"
MODEL=""  # session model supplied by user, e.g. gpt-6.1-sol; empty means unknown
MODEL_REASONING_EFFORT=""  # session effort supplied by user, e.g. medium; empty means unknown
REPAIR_REPORT="artifacts/${RUN_ID}/chunking-repair/report.json"
```

Record the repairing session separately from the reviewer. In REPAIR_REPORT, use
repairer={"kind":"agent","name":"Codex","model":MODEL,
"model_reasoning_effort":MODEL_REASONING_EFFORT,"launch_mode":"manual_workflow"}.
These variables describe the selected session; they do not change its settings.
Use user-confirmed values and null for unknowns; never infer from workflow.json
or a model-family self-description. If launched by a controller, use its resolved
settings and launch_mode instead. Do not add settings_source or session_id.
Preserve prior repair attribution when extending an existing report. Never replace
reviewer attribution with repairer attribution. Include originating review/report
paths, cause, changes, tests, blockers and rebuild commands in the repair report
and summarize the model, reasoning effort and launch mode in the final response.
Use exact recorded report paths for other artifact layouts.

Read artifacts/${RUN_ID}/chunking-review/review.json and report.json,
chunking bundles, originals, and available state.json/repair-task.json.
Use exact recorded paths for other layouts or build IDs; record actual model/settings.

1. Read gates/findings and reproduce failures against originals; identify the earliest
underlying defect. Pending inspection needs evidence, stale reviews need matching
inputs/fresh review. Record source-located counterevidence for disputed findings.

Trace chunks through evidence IDs and parsed elements to originals/PDF layout.
Check sentence/list integrity, governing context, tables, citations, size boundaries
and duplicates. Preserve genuine repetition at distinct locations; never invent
missing text or treat diagram labels as authoritative prose.

2. Apply the smallest generic code/configuration fix; preserve unrelated changes.
Add/run targeted offline regression tests; mock model-backed behavior. Never edit
source text, editions, frozen bundles, judgments or state. Never discard findings,
lower thresholds, hard-code document/page exceptions or fabricate approval.

3. Report cause, changes, tests, blockers and exact rebuild commands. Rebuild only
when separately authorized. Follow controller archival/downstream invalidation rules;
code/config/source/model changes require repair from ingestion or a fresh run.
Retain compatible caches; reject stale approvals. Respect retry/time limits; escalate
ambiguity, scope expansion or repeated lack of progress. No paid calls, increased
budgets, publication, commits or pushes without separate authorization.

After authorized rebuilds, request fresh independent agent_prompt_chunking_review.
Never approve your repair or transfer judgments to changed outputs. Fixture tests
are not pilot approval. Finish with the next action.
